    # ------------------------------------------------------------------ 13. Paper 3
    lesson(
        module=M_EXAM, topic="Paper 3",
        title="Paper 3: planning and doing the practical",
        slug="fdn3-exam-paper-3-practical",
        minutes=25,
        summary="Paper 3 tests hands-on skills in two compulsory questions; plan the menu, write a work plan and time plan, follow a sensible order of work, keep hygiene and safety, serve the food well and evaluate the result.",
        objectives=[
            "Describe Paper 3: two compulsory practical questions testing hands-on skills",
            "Write a work plan and a time plan for a short practical",
            "Put tasks in a sensible order of work, doing long and cold tasks at the right time",
            "Follow hygiene and safety rules, serve neatly and evaluate the result",
        ],
        key_concepts=["Paper 3", "Work plan", "Time plan", "Order of work", "Dovetailing", "Hygiene", "Serving", "Evaluation"],
        blocks=[
            H("Introduction"),
            T("A girl in a school kitchen is told to prepare and serve a meal. She starts by chopping onions, then realises the rice needs 20 minutes and "
              "the stove is not lit. By the time she has finished, the fish is cold. The Board's 2023 report says that Paper 3 had **two compulsory "
              "questions** testing practical skills through hands-on activities, and that knowing the principles is not enough to score well. "
              "The report advises teachers to intensify practical work, and students to work in groups and relate what they learn to society. "
              "Planning is the secret of a smooth practical."),
            D("According to the Board's 2023 report, **Paper 3 had two compulsory questions** testing practical (psychomotor) skills. "
              "The details (time, marks, the form of the planning sheets) are given by your teacher or the Board. Check the exact format with your teacher.", title="Paper 3 facts"),
            H("1. Read the task and plan the menu"),
            T("Read the whole task twice. Note the number of people, the type of dishes, the time allowed, the ingredients given and any special instructions. "
              "Choose dishes that you can cook well in the time, that use the ingredients supplied, and that give a balance of colour, flavour and texture."),
            H("2. The work plan"),
            D("A **work plan** is a list of the jobs to be done, in order, with the equipment and ingredients needed for each. A **time plan** shows when each job starts and finishes, "
              "so that all dishes are ready and hot (or cold) at serving time.", title="Work plan and time plan"),
            KEY("Rules for the order of work",
                "These rules save time and produce better food.",
                cards=[["Start with long jobs", "Put rice, beans or stews that need a long time on first."],
                       ["Cold jobs early", "Make cold dishes (fruit salad, a cold drink) first and keep them cool and covered."],
                       ["Dovetail", "While one dish cooks, prepare another. Dovetailing means fitting jobs together so that no time is wasted."],
                       ["Prepare before cooking", "Wash, peel and cut together by type. Collect equipment and ingredients before you start."],
                       ["Finish with the delicate dishes", "Fry fish and dish up near the end so they are hot and crisp."],
                       ["Clear as you go", "Wash used utensils when you have a moment, and keep your work place tidy."]]),
            IMG("f5fdn3-paper3-timeplan.svg",
                alt="A time plan chart for a 120-minute practical showing five jobs as bars: preparation, fruit salad, stew, rice and fish, then serving and clearing.",
                caption="Figure 1. A sample time plan (invented for practice). Each bar shows when a job starts and ends."),
            CODE("Time   Job\n0:00  Wash hands, collect equipment and ingredients, light the stove\n0:10  Prepare fruit salad, cover and keep cool\n0:25  Wash and chop onions, tomatoes and pepper; season the fish\n0:40  Start the tomato stew and simmer\n0:55  Wash rice and put it on to cook (until about 1:20)\n1:05  Fry the fish\n1:20  Dish up, garnish, set the table\n1:35  Serve and eat\n1:45  Clear, wash up and clean the work place",
                 "text", title="A sample time plan for a meal (invented for practice)"),
            H("3. Hygiene, safety and skills"),
            KEY("What the examiner looks for",
                "Marks are given for skills, not only for the food. Follow the kitchen rules in the earlier modules.",
                cards=[["Personal hygiene", "Clean overall or apron, hair covered, nails short, hands washed before starting and after raw meat or fish."],
                       ["Food hygiene", "Separate raw and cooked foods, clean boards and knives, cover food, taste with a clean spoon."],
                       ["Safety", "Handles turned inward, dry hands on hot dishes, cloths away from flame, careful with oil and hot water."],
                       ["Skills", "Neat cutting, correct cooking methods, seasoning, timing and economy (no waste)."],
                       ["Tidiness", "Clean work surface, used utensils washed, sink and stove cleaned at the end."]]),
            H("4. Serving and evaluating"),
            T("Serve the food at the right temperature, neatly arranged on clean dishes, with a garnish. Serve hot food hot. Put the dishes on a clean tray "
              "or a laid table, as asked. Afterwards, **evaluate**: say what went well, what went wrong and why, and how you would improve it. "
              "For example, 'the fish was slightly overcooked because I fried it too early; next time I will start it five minutes later'. Honest "
              "evaluation shows understanding."),
            TIP("Paper 3 is hands-on, so practise in the kitchen as often as you can, ideally with a timer. Write the plan for each practice and compare it with what happened.", title="Exam link"),
            EX("Worked example 1: order the jobs",
               intro="A practical asks for boiled rice, fish stew and fruit salad. Put these jobs in a good order: fry onions for the stew; wash fruit and cut for the salad; cook the rice; light the stove; serve; make the stew.",
               steps=[
                   S("Start", text="Light the stove and collect equipment. Wash hands."),
                   S("Cold dish first", text="Cut the fruit salad early, cover and keep cool."),
                   S("Long jobs next", text="Start the stew (fry onions, add tomato, fish) and simmer."),
                   S("Dovetail", text="While the stew simmers, cook the rice."),
                   S("Finish", text="Dish up everything and serve hot."),
               ]),
            EX("Worked example 2: check the time plan",
               intro="Using the sample time plan, how long does the rice cook, and how long between dishing up and finishing the whole practical?",
               steps=[
                   S("Rice", text="It goes on at 0:55 and is ready about 1:20. That is 25 minutes."),
                   S("Dishing up to the end", text="Dishing up starts at 1:20 and clearing finishes at 2:00 (the end). That is 40 minutes."),
                   S("Check the total", text="0:00 to 2:00 is 120 minutes, as planned."),
               ]),
            MISTAKE("Not writing a plan at all",
                    "Candidates who start cooking at once often finish late or serve cold food. Spend the first minutes on a short plan."),
            MISTAKE("Forgetting hygiene and clearing",
                    "A good dish with a dirty work place or unwashed hands loses marks. Hygiene and tidiness are part of the task."),
            MISTAKE("Serving too early or too late",
                    "Time your dishes to finish together. Hot dishes should not stand while others finish."),
            QUIZ("Why do we start long-cooking dishes first?",
                 ["So they are ready together with the quicker dishes", "Because they are easier", "So they can be eaten before the others", "Because the stove is cold at first"], 0,
                 "Starting long jobs first allows other dishes to be done while they cook, so everything finishes together.",
                 hint="Think of how to finish everything at the same time.",
                 feedback=["", "Ease is not the reason.", "All dishes are served together.", "Stove temperature is not the principle."]),
            QUIZ("What does 'dovetailing' mean in a practical?",
                 ["Fitting jobs together so no time is wasted", "Cutting food into wedges", "Doing one job at a time", "Serving in a fan shape"], 0,
                 "Dovetailing means fitting jobs together, for example preparing vegetables while rice cooks.",
                 hint="Think of how two pieces fit together.",
                 feedback=["", "This is not about shapes.", "That is the opposite of dovetailing.", "This is not about serving shapes."]),
            PQ("What is the difference between a work plan and a time plan?",
               "A work plan lists the jobs in order with the equipment and ingredients. A time plan shows the time each job starts and ends so everything is ready together."),
            PQ("State five rules of hygiene to follow before and during a practical.",
               "Wash hands; wear a clean apron; cover the hair; keep nails short and clean; cover cuts; use clean utensils; keep raw and cooked foods apart; use a clean spoon to taste."),
            PQ("A practical begins at 9:00 and ends at 11:00. Rice takes 25 minutes and is put on at 10:05. At what time will it be ready and how long before the end of the practical?",
               "10:05 + 25 minutes = 10:30. The practical ends at 11:00, so the rice is ready 30 minutes before the end."),
            PQ("Write a short evaluation of a practical in which the stew was too salty.",
               "The stew was too salty because I added salt twice without tasting. Next time I will add salt a little at a time and taste with a clean spoon before adding more."),
            SUM("Paper 3 has two compulsory practical questions testing hands-on skills (Board 2023 report); check the format with your teacher.",
                "Read the task, choose the menu, write a work plan and a time plan.",
                "Order of work: long jobs first, cold dishes early, dovetail, delicate dishes last.",
                "Follow hygiene and safety rules; serve neatly at the right temperature.",
                "Evaluate honestly: what went well, what went wrong, and how to improve."),
        ],
    ),
